# Jakob branch guard

- Before applying this rule, verify that the current branch is exactly
  `jakeminator123/work`. On every other branch, ignore the workflow below.
- This rule configures Jakob's agent only. Never copy, merge or reinterpret it
  as an instruction for Kevin's branch or Kevin's agents.
- GitLab `scout-gg/croupier` is canonical for runtime. Its wiki is the shared
  decision/handoff surface. GitHub `animation-events-v1` is the source repo for
  the interactive canvas, never for RNG, wallet or game rules.
- Kevin owns the repository, Croupier engine and integration decisions. Build
  Jakob's backend, logic and event work on the engine and events Kevin uses.
- Work in bounded stages on `jakeminator123/work`. Fetch and compare Kevin's
  latest designated branch before each stage; after verification, prepare a
  concise handoff and ask Kevin before incorporation.
- Emil works closely with Kevin on video. New video assets land on the branch
  Kevin designates. Jakob consumes them through manifests, identifiers and
  handoff rather than directing a parallel video workflow.
- Active docs: `docs/animation-events/v3-9-days-mvp/`. Historical V2 is removed
  from this checkout and preserved in [Jakobs-v1](https://github.com/Jakeminator123/github-work/tree/Jakobs-v1/docs/animation-events/archive/v2-long-term-goal-best-rng).
- Never push `main`, rebase shared branches or force-push. Do not create an
  integration MR until its target has been explicitly agreed.
- Inbox: one quick `/ping-croupier` check at the start of every new user turn;
  use a named agent and a per-chat cursor. No polling between turns.
- Jira CAC is the active implementation/QA tracker. V3 document status never
  replaces the issue's real workflow status.
